                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Bloody Trapland 2 is a pretty damn good difficult platformer. It's not a masterpiece, but if you're into challenging platformers, I think you'll have a good time with it.\r\n\r\nThe movement is a little janky and takes some getting used to at first, but I think it's more part of the game's charm than anything. There's actual skill involved, and you're not constantly fighting the controls. The game is a huge improvement over the first one in pretty much every way: the mechanics are more refined, there are new movement mechanics, the level design is much better, the levels are harder in a way that actually feels fun, and the graphical style is obviously a lot better. After playing both games back-to-back, the difference is very apparent. \r\nIt's just a fun, challenging game. 8/10.",
